    description: "**Found via self-analysis dogfooding on 2026-05-17 (round 17), via baseline-comparison-across-time.**\n\n**Symptom.** On hypergumbo's self-analysis, 4 of 6 registered framework linkers emit symbols but produce ZERO edges from their own origin. The detected symbols are connected to the call graph (other origins reference them), but the linkers themselves contribute no relationship edges — which is the whole point of a framework-aware linker.\n\n**Baseline comparison (Apr 23 → May 16/17):**\n\n| linker | Apr 23 edges from origin | May 17 edges from origin | duration_ms (May 17) |\n|---|---:|---:|---:|\n| event-sourcing-linker-v1 | 34 | **0** | 2,523 |\n| http-linker-v1 | 22 | **0** | 2,750 |\n| graphql-resolver-linker-v1 | 19 | **0** | 2,482 |\n| database-query-linker-v1 | 35 | **0** | 2,299 |\n| message-queue-linker-v1 | 156 | 103 | 3,373 |\n| websocket-linker-v1 | (n/a, kind: websocket_endpoint) | 20 | 2,263 |\n\nTotal wall-clock spent producing 0 edges: **~10 seconds** on this codebase per `hypergumbo run` invocation. Across 4 linkers, this is pure waste.\n\n**Reproduction.**\n\n```bash\nhypergumbo run --out /tmp/r17.json --no-sketch-fan-out --no-handler-slices .\n\npython3 -c \"\nimport json\nfrom collections import Counter\nd = json.load(open('/tmp/r17.json'))\nlinkers = ['event-sourcing-linker-v1', 'message-queue-linker-v1',\n           'websocket-linker-v1', 'http-linker-v1',\n           'graphql-resolver-linker-v1', 'database-query-linker-v1']\nfor ln in linkers:\n    nodes = sum(1 for n in d['nodes'] if n.get('origin') == ln)\n    edges = sum(1 for e in d['edges'] if e.get('origin') == ln)\n    print(f'{ln}: nodes={nodes}, edges={edges}')\n\"\n```\n\nOutput:\n```\nevent-sourcing-linker-v1: nodes=14, edges=0\nmessage-queue-linker-v1: nodes=75, edges=103\nwebsocket-linker-v1: nodes=23, edges=20\nhttp-linker-v1: nodes=0, edges=0\ngraphql-resolver-linker-v1: nodes=11, edges=0\ndatabase-query-linker-v1: nodes=34, edges=0\n```\n\n**Where the regression appears tied to schema migration.** Between Apr 23 (schema 0.2.2) and May 16 (schema 0.8.0), the data model changed:\n\n- 13 framework-specific node kinds vanished (db_query, http_client, websocket_endpoint, mq_publisher, mq_subscriber, event_publisher, event_subscriber, graphql_resolver, subprocess_call, devDependency, module_file, npm_package, tsconfig).\n- Some were folded into function-kind nodes with `meta.framework_role` (146 nodes still carry this).\n- New kinds appeared: `call_site` (111), `external_symbol` (1561), `variable` (1487).\n- 17 evidence_types collapsed (many `unresolved_*` and `function_call` types replaced by a single `ast_call` bucket of 19,957 edges).\n\n**Hypothesis.** During the schema 0.2.2 → 0.8.0 migration, 4 framework linkers (event-sourcing, http, graphql-resolver, database-query) had their NODE-emission paths refactored (the kinds were merged) but their EDGE-emission paths were not migrated. They still scan files (taking 2-3 seconds each) but their downstream edge-construction code targets the OLD node kinds that no longer exist.\n\nCompare to message-queue-linker-v1 (still produces edges) and websocket-linker-v1 (still produces edges) — these two were apparently migrated correctly.\n\n**Severity.** Medium — coverage regression for security-claim and dataflow tooling. The whole point of a `database-query-linker` is to link queries to their callers (so `verify-claims` can ask \"what reaches the SQL boundary?\"). With 34 db_query call_sites detected but 0 connecting edges, the SQL nodes are present but disconnected from the call graph.\n\n**Investigation actions.**\n\n1. Read each of the 4 dead linkers (event_sourcing.py, http.py, graphql_resolver.py, database_query.py) and compare to message_queue.py / websocket.py to find what edge-construction patterns were updated for the new schema.\n2. Confirm whether the missing edges are \"edges from linker origin pointing into the call graph\" or \"edges with linker-set meta but other origin\".\n3. The wasted 10s of compute (4 linkers × 2-3s each) is a hidden performance cost — fixing edge production or skipping the linker entirely both resolve this.\n\n**Cross-references.**\n- INV-sopon (linker-synthesized symbols missing origin stamp) — separate aspect of linker output quality.\n- WI-fozoh (external_symbol synthesis: stable_id/canonical_name null) — adjacent.\n- WI-higap (425 edges missing origin_run_id) — related to origin-stamp gaps.\n- R17 baseline comparison surfaced this: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/self-analysis-baselines/ has Apr 5, Apr 21, Apr 23, May 16 snapshots.\n\n**Notebook reference.** `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/notebookjournal_05162026_0438.md` Round 17 section."  # 921c
    fields:  # 921c
      statement: "Framework linkers must produce relationship edges, not just symbol nodes — connecting framework concepts (mq_publisher → mq_subscriber, route → handler, db_query → caller) is their entire purpose. Currently event-sourcing-linker-v1, http-linker-v1, graphql-resolver-linker-v1, and database-query-linker-v1 each scan 310-817 files in 2-3 seconds and produce 0 edges from their own origin. Compared to Apr 23 baseline (schema 0.2.2): event-sourcing dropped 34→0 edges, http-linker 22→0, graphql-resolver 19→0, database-query 35→0. message-queue and websocket linkers still produce edges correctly."  # 921c
      root_cause: "Hypothesized: between schema 0.2.2 (Apr 23) and schema 0.8.0 (May 16), the data model refactor merged 13 framework-specific node kinds (db_query, http_client, mq_publisher, event_publisher, etc.) into a smaller set (function with meta.framework_role, call_site with meta.call_kind). The 4 broken linkers had their NODE-emission paths migrated to the new shape but their EDGE-construction code still targets old kind names that no longer exist. message-queue-linker and websocket-linker apparently received the full migration. Fix: audit each of the 4 broken linkers (event_sourcing.py, http.py, graphql_resolver.py, database_query.py) against message_queue.py and websocket.py to find the missing edge-construction update. Verify by re-running self-analysis and confirming non-zero edge counts from each linker origin."  # 921c
